.TH SING-ALONG 1 "2026" "sing-along 2.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sing-along \- synced lyrics for your own music files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sing-along
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sing-along
is a desktop music player with synced lyrics. Run with no arguments it opens the
player window. Run with a command it works headless, which is what scripts and
coding agents use.
.PP
Lyrics are fetched from LRCLIB, with an optional NetEase fallback, and written as
a sidecar file next to the audio.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B fetch \fIpath\fR...
Download lyrics for every audio file under the given paths and write them as
\fB.lrc\fR beside each track. Files that already have lyrics are counted as
skipped rather than re-downloaded.
.TP
.B export \fIpath\fR...
Write the lyrics that are already present in one specific player's format. Which
format is right depends on the player and is not interchangeable; see
\fBFORMATS\fR below.
.TP
.B status \fIpath\fR...
Report each file as \fBsynced\fR (timed lyrics), \fBplain\fR (text but no timing)
or \fBnone\fR, then a summary. Run this before \fBfetch\fR to see what is actually
missing.
.TP
.B formats
List the players \fBexport\fR understands.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS fetch
.TP
.BI \-\-script " off|simplified|traditional"
Convert Chinese lyrics to the given script while writing. Off by default.
Conversion is lossy, so it is only worth doing when the lyrics are in the other
script.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Re-download even where a lyric file already exists.
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy " url"
Send lyric requests through this proxy. Without it the app connects directly;
it deliberately does not inherit \fBHTTP_PROXY\fR from the environment, which is
usually set for other tooling.
.SS export
.TP
.BI \-\-for " player"
Target player, for example \fBsteve\fR or \fBgramophone\fR. See \fBFORMATS\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " a2|lrc|ttml|txt"
Explicit format instead of \fB\-\-for\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print what would be written without writing anything.
.SH FORMATS
Word-level lyric files are not portable: each player reads one dialect and shows
the others as literal text.
.TP
.B steve, apple, ios
TTML. Steve on iOS highlights words only from TTML; its LRC reader is line-level
and does not strip tags, so enhanced LRC appears as timestamps inside the lyrics.
.TP
.B gramophone, fluxio, android
Enhanced LRC (A2), the \fB<mm:ss.xx>word\fR extension.
.TP
.B lrc
Plain line-level LRC, for any reader.
.TP
.B txt
Plain text, no timing.
.PP
Booming (Android) is not supported. Its parser inserts a space after every
non-final word regardless of script, so Chinese renders as a spaced-out line. No
file format avoids that.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An operation failed; the reason is printed.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown command or malformed arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
Fetch missing lyrics for a library, converting to Simplified Chinese:
.PP
.RS 4
sing-along fetch ~/Music --script simplified
.RE
.PP
Export for an iPhone, previewing first:
.PP
.RS 4
sing-along export ~/Music --for steve --dry-run
.RE
.PP
Check what a folder is missing:
.PP
.RS 4
sing-along status ~/Music
.RE
.SH SKILLS
A skill file describing the recommended workflow for a coding agent ships at
\fB/usr/share/sing-along/skills/sing-along/SKILL.md\fR. It covers the questions to
settle first, the player-to-format mapping, how to verify a converted file, and
the rules that matter (never rewrite lyric text; do not claim a track can be
synced when only unsynchronised text exists).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/app.singalong.desktop/
Database, settings, cached album covers.
.TP
.B <track>.lrc
Lyric sidecar written beside the audio file.
.SH SEE ALSO
The player's Settings dialog documents the proxy and Chinese script options.
